- How would you scale the provenance store to 10M events/day?
- How do you enforce tamper-evidence across regional replicas?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical ability to design per-tenant budgets with latency guarantees, bursts, and data locality in a production-grade LLM gateway.

## Key Concepts

- Token bucket and backpressure
- Budget drift detection and alerting
- Regional data locality and routing
- Canary routing and model variant selection based on budget state

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal per-tenant token bucket (conceptual)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate; this.capacity = capacity; this.tokens = capacity; this.last = Date.now();
  }
  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const add = (now - this.last) * this.rate / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + add);
    this.last = now;
  }
  consume(n = 1) {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate budgets against real traffic with drift scenarios?
- What observability would you add to detect bursts without SLA violations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world hybrid edge-cloud serving with data locality, SLA management, and per-tenant isolation under fluctuating network conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Data locality and residency per tenant
- Edge vs cloud routing and burst handling
- Per-tenant model pools and versioning
- Observability, fault tolerance, and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluator
function routeRequest(req, policyStore){
  const p = policyStore.get(req.tenantId);
  if(p.locality === 'edge' && req.latencyBudget >= EDGE_LATENCY){
    return 'edge';
  }
  return 'cloud';
}
```

